    "Simulation is active. ThermalPilot does not control heating.": "Simulace aktivní. ThermalPilot neřídí topení.",
    "Observation and learning only; no thermostat control.": "Jen pozorování a učení; bez řízení.",
    "ThermalPilot controls thermostat targets.": "ThermalPilot řídí cíle termostatů.",
    "Seasonal fallback temperatures are used.": "Použity sezónní záložní teploty.",
    "Scheduled targets remain simulated; season transitions can change thermostat targets.": "Plán simulovaný; sezóny mohou změnit skutečné cíle.",
    "Live thermostat control is not enabled.": "Skutečné řízení nezapnuto.",
    "Target changes include the shared start/stop offsets. The temperature forecast models the planned heating period; actual valve and heat-pump delays must be checked against observations.": "Obsahuje posuny začátku/konce. Ověřte skutečné zpoždění ventilů a čerpadla.",
    "These forecasts were saved 1, 3 or 6 hours before the measurements. Later readings do not change them. Lower error is better; compare it with simply predicting no temperature change. Different heating, computers and other heat sources can affect the result.": "Předpovědi uloženy 1, 3 či 6 hodin předem, později neměnné. Menší odchylka lepší; srovnejte se stálou teplotou. Jiné teplo ovlivňuje výsledek.",
    "Compare recorded temperatures with forecasts saved hours earlier. The accuracy cards also compare against predicting no temperature change. Forecasts assume the proposed heating plan; actual heating may differ, especially during simulation.": "Srovnejte s dřívějšími předpověďmi a stálou teplotou. Skutečné topení se může lišit, zvlášť v simulaci.",
    "Forecasts are compared with measurements within five minutes of their due time. “Similar heating” means observed demand matched the forecast for at least 90% of observations, with no large recording gaps. These counts give context, not a guarantee of accuracy.": "Měření do pěti minut. Podobné topení: ≥90% shoda bez velkých mezer. Počty nezaručují přesnost.",
    "Each row shows the latest observation within its 15-minute interval, not an average. Suggested thermostat target is the setting ThermalPilot would apply, not a room-temperature forecast. Table shows up to 288 intervals. Original observations remain stored internally. Short chart views use 15-minute time labels; longer views use wider intervals.": "Poslední pozorování za 15 minut, ne průměr. Cíl je nastavení, ne předpověď. Až 288 intervalů; originály zůstávají.",
    "Suggested On means the boosted target window, including valve timing offsets. Relay On means observed demand; it does not guarantee heat flow.": "Navržené zapnutí je zvýšený cíl s posuny ventilů. Relé ukazuje požadavek, ne zaručené teplo.",
    ", without heating, remaining slab warmth or appliance heat. Lower temperature loss means slower modeled cooling. This is a model estimate, not measured energy efficiency or an insulation rating.": ", bez topení, zbytkového tepla či spotřebičů. Menší ztráta je pomalejší modelové chladnutí, ne hodnocení energie či izolace.",
    "Cooling-speed bands are provisional: under 1 h, 1–2 h, 2–4 h, 4–8 h, and 8 h or longer per 1°C drop. For a selected house type, badges instead compare with that type: under 0.5×, 0.5–0.8×, 0.8–1.25×, 1.25–2×, and at least 2× its reference cooling time. Initial rooms share starting estimates and remain unrated. Comparisons become more useful as their heat-loss parameters adapt to observations. Wind, ventilation, sensor placement and unmeasured heat sources can affect the estimates. The listed time describes this reference test, not how long heating can safely remain off in your home.": "Počáteční modely stejné. Vítr, větrání, senzory a jiné teplo ovlivňují srovnání. Referenční čas není bezpečná doba vypnutí.",
    "Learned parameters and season aggregates are retained when old observations are compacted.": "Naučené parametry a sezónní součty zůstávají při kompresi.",
    "Open a Home Assistant dashboard once, then return here to load embedded history cards.": "Otevřete panel Home Assistant a vraťte se pro historii.",
    "Water-based systems only: raise the thermostat target this many minutes before the planned heat-delivery session, allowing slow valves to open. Electric and air distribution ignore this setting and use no advance offset.": "Jen voda: zvýšit předem pro pomalé ventily. Elektřina/vzduch ignorují posun.",
    "Water-based systems only: lower the thermostat target this many minutes before the planned heat-delivery session ends, allowing valves to close. Electric and air distribution ignore this setting and use no closing offset.": "Jen voda: snížit před koncem pro ventily. Elektřina/vzduch ignorují posun.",
    "What produces heat for your house. Select air-to-water for your water floor system supplied by an air-source heat pump. Gas, oil, wood and district heating need their own fuel-cost logic; choosing a house detail does not yet enable a different controller or reset learned room data.": "Zdroj domu. Paliva nedostanou vlastní cenové řízení; data zůstávají.",
    "How heat reaches rooms: circulating water in floors or radiators, electric floor/ceiling/panels, or warm air. Mixed means different rooms use different systems. Water distribution can optionally use a heating-water sensor and uses valve timing. Electric and warm-air distribution ignore those inputs and learn response from observed thermostat demand. Mixed and Other retain water requirements until room overrides are supported.": "Voda používá časy ventilů a volitelný senzor. Elektřina/vzduch učí z požadavku. Smíšené zachová vodní nastavení.",
    "The construction around floor heating, which affects how slowly heat is stored and released. Concrete slab describes your heated floor. Choose Not applicable if there is no floor heating. This does not change your configured response lag or erase learned parameters.": "Podlaha ovlivňuje akumulaci. Bez podlahového topení: Nevztahuje se. Nemění zpoždění ani model.",
    "The structure below your home: slab on ground, crawl space or basement. A heated concrete floor can be above a basement, so this is separate from Heated floor. Choose Unknown if unsure. This descriptive setting does not reset observation history or learned models.": "Základy oddělené od podlahy. Při nejistotě Neznámé. Modely a historie zůstávají.",
    "Sunlight through large windows, especially south-facing windows, can warm a room. No additional physical solar heating system is needed. Select the main direction of those windows to enable solar estimates, or Solar heating off to turn them off. Home Assistant’s location determines seasonal sun elevation and azimuth; cloud conditions come from your weather source. The effect starts at zero and learns gradually. Missing sunlight data assumes no solar warmth; room temperature limits still apply.": "Slunce velkými okny, solární systém netřeba. Směr, poloha a oblačnost dávají přínos, učený od nuly. Bez dat žádné solární teplo; meze platí.",
    "Clear means the windows receive direct sunlight without major obstructions. Choose Partly shaded for some trees, buildings or overhangs, or Mostly shaded when sunlight is usually blocked. Forecasts use a more cautious solar allowance: partly shaded uses 65% and mostly shaded 30% of the clear allowance. Actual room warming is still learned from observations; no solar heat is assumed before learning. Seasonal leaf cover and changing shading can still affect accuracy.": "Bez, částečně či převážně zastíněné: 100%, 65% či 30% solárního přínosu. Skutečné teplo učené; stín se mění.",
    "Optional local wind sensor, for example sensor.netatmo_tuuli_ms using m/s. Valid readings are averaged over the last 30 minutes. ThermalPilot learns a separate wind effect only after enough varied observations; no fixed wind penalty is assumed. Missing, invalid or unchanged-for-two-hours readings are ignored, and normal temperature-based planning and heating continue. Fresh wind correction gradually returns to typical conditions in forecasts further ahead. A stable calm reading may also be ignored conservatively. Units are detected automatically.": "Volitelný vítr, automatické jednotky, průměr 30 min. Efekt učený z různých dat. Chybějící, neplatný či 2 h stálý ignorován; topení pokračuje. Dálková předpověď jde k běžnému větru.",
    "Emergency lower temperature limit shared by all rooms. Each room’s own target is the normal comfort goal. ThermalPilot prioritizes avoiding this limit even when electricity is expensive; this value is not the idle thermostat target.": "Absolutní dolní mez, ne klidový cíl. Cíl místnosti komfort; mez chráněna i v drahých hodinách.",
    "Upper temperature limit shared by all rooms. Extra heating and heat storage must stay within this limit.": "Horní mez všech místností; extra teplo nesmí nad ni.",
    "Optional sensor with forecast timestamp/value entries, such as Nordpool Predict FI. Only relative expensive/cheap patterns after confirmed prices are used, so no forecast price unit or additional costs are required. The Source price unit setting applies only to the confirmed total-price sensor. An expensive upcoming period can increase the heat reserve at the end of the known-price plan. Forecast prices are not compared directly with your total prices, used as confirmed prices or used to execute future heating commands. Missing forecasts keep normal planning. Confirmed prices always determine the executable schedule.": "Volitelný relativní trend po potvrzených cenách. Jednotky a přirážky netřeba. Může zvýšit zásobu, nikdy potvrzená cena či přímý budoucí příkaz. Chybí: běžný plán.",
    "Notify in Home Assistant when a room temperature sensor stays unchanged or unavailable for this many hours. A stable room can also have an unchanged reading, so the warning asks you to check the sensor. ThermalPilot sends at most one sensor notification per calendar day. Monitoring runs while ThermalPilot is active; long monitoring gaps restart the timer.": "Varovat po této době bez nové teploty.",
    "Summer fallback always applies from 15.5. through 30.9. Outside those dates, it also applies when the day’s lowest forecast temperature is equal to or above this value. For example, a setting of 6°C means the daily minimum must be at least 6°C for ThermalPilot to use summer fallback temperatures. Lower readings already observed that day are included. If a full-day forecast is unavailable outside the summer dates, winter fallback is used.": "Letní záloha 15.5.–30.9., jinak při denním minimu nad mezí. Chybějící předpověď mimo data neaktivuje léto.",
    "Negative values reduce estimated heat loss while the fireplace is active; −20% means a 20% reduction.": "Záporné snižuje ztrátu při krbu; −20% je o 20% méně.",
    "Prefer a sensor that includes electricity prices and additional costs, such as VAT, transfer tariffs, electricity tax and retailer margin. A variable electricity-price sensor without these costs also works. If transfer tariffs differ between day and night, including them helps ThermalPilot choose the cheapest heating hours; omitting them can shift heating to hours that are less economical overall. Select a source containing today/tomorrow or timestamped raw_today/raw_tomorrow price lists, and choose the matching source price unit.": "Vhodná celková cena s daní, sítí a marží. Proměnlivá cena samotná funguje; chybějící denní/noční síťové sazby mohou zhoršit volbu hodin. Použijte today/tomorrow či datované raw_today/raw_tomorrow a správnou jednotku.",
    "Hourly average uses fixed hourly averages of the source prices. 15 minutes plans using quarter-hour intervals. Flexible builds heating sessions in 15-minute steps, allowing runs such as 60 or 75 minutes while respecting the minimum flexible heating run.": "Hodinový průměr, 15 min interval či pružné kroky 15 min s minimem.",
    "The shortest planned heating session in flexible scheduling mode. Longer sessions can be chosen in 15-minute steps. This setting applies to flexible runs; valve opening and closing offsets are applied separately.": "Nejkratší pružná fáze; delší po 15 min.",
    "Initial estimate of how slowly heat input affects room temperature and how long its effect persists. Concrete slabs often need a longer delay, but lightweight floors, radiators, electric heaters and air systems also have a response time. Use a shorter value for faster systems. This remains relevant to every distribution; it is separate from valve opening or closing time.": "Počáteční odhad setrvačnosti a doznívání; model se učí.",
    "The warm outdoor endpoint of the initial heating-hours curve. At this temperature or warmer, the starting model assumes the lower daily heating need. This curve seeds the model before enough real heating and cooling observations are available.": "Teplý bod počáteční denní potřeby; skutečná odezva učená.",
    "The cold outdoor endpoint of the initial heating-hours curve. At this temperature or colder, the starting model assumes the higher daily heating need. Set it below the warm endpoint. Actual room response is learned from observations.": "Studený bod pod teplým; skutečná odezva učená.",
    "Allows real thermostat setpoint changes when ThermalPilot changes between Active and Passive. Active applies each room’s target temperature; Passive applies the seasonal fallback: the shared summer setpoint or each room’s normal target in winter. These commands can occur even with simulation enabled. This does not enable live heating schedule control.": "Skutečné sezónní změny i v simulaci. Aktivní: cíl místnosti; pasivní: letní/zimní záloha. Neřízení rozvrhu.",
    "The thermostat target used for all configured rooms while ThermalPilot is Passive, if real Active/Passive season setpoint control is enabled. A low summer target normally prevents heating without switching off the thermostats.": "Společný letní cíl při pasivním sezónním řízení. Nízký cíl obvykle zabrání topení bez vypnutí termostatů.",
    "Degrees added to each room’s target temperature during a suggested heating window. For example, a 20 °C target with a 1.5 °C boost suggests a 21.5 °C thermostat setpoint to store heat. Scheduled targets remain simulated in this version.": "Stupně nad cílem pro akumulaci, např. 20 + 1,5 = 21,5°C.",
    "Negative values temporarily lower the thermostat target during expensive electricity hours. After a planned heating session, ThermalPilot first restores the room’s normal target. It then chooses reduction only when predicted stored warmth can avoid thermostat heating while supporting room comfort. For example, −1°C allows a 20°C target to be reduced to 19°C during selected costly hours. The reduced target never goes below Minimum allowed temperature. Normal target is restored when reduction is no longer useful; a new planned heating session uses the boosted target. Duration is chosen by the plan, not a fixed number of hours.": "Záporné snížení v drahých hodinách s dostatkem zásoby. Po fázi nejprve běžný cíl, nikdy pod minimum. Obnova když nepotřebné; délka dle plánu.",
    "Select the measured supply-water temperature. A temperature sensor uses its state; a climate entity uses its current_temperature attribute. This is the measured water temperature, not the thermostat’s target. Optional for water-based systems. A valid reading adjusts the estimated heating output. Without it, planning and learning continue from observed thermostat demand, without a water-temperature adjustment. Missing readings do not force fallback targets.": "Volitelná měřená přívodní voda; climate používá current_temperature, ne cíl. Koriguje výkon. Chybění nezastaví učení/plán ani nevynutí zálohu.",
    "Simulation calculates heating suggestions without applying scheduled targets. Disable simulation and confirm to enable real thermostat control. If another automation controls these thermostats, disable it first. Observation and learning continue in both modes.": "Simulace nepoužívá plánované cíle. Vypnout a potvrdit pro řízení; vypněte jinou související automatizaci, pokud existuje. Učení v obou režimech.",
    "Choose the interface language. Room and entity names remain unchanged. Save settings to keep the choice. Embedded history cards follow this choice where supported by Home Assistant.": "Zvolte jazyk a uložte. Názvy zůstávají. Vložená historie následuje dle podpory.",
    "All room timelines share the price chart’s time axis.${zones.length?' Zone rows show recorded heating and cooling only; off and standby periods stay empty. Plan adds suggested heating only for tariff-optimized zones.':''} Teal shows the suggested thermostat boost window; amber shows observed heating demand. ": "Společná osa. Tyrkys: zvýšení; oranžová: pozorovaný požadavek. ",
    "The selected period controls past history. Today and tomorrow are included when prices are published. Recorded activity is shown before now; future suggestions follow the current plan. Price gaps stay empty. ": "Období určuje historii; dnes/zítra s cenami. Před nyní pozorování; poté plán. Cenové mezery prázdné. ",
    "Times align to 15-minute boundaries; wider views show fewer labels. Hover, focus or tap a price bar or heating period for details.": "Meze 15 min; delší pohled méně popisků. Najeďte, zaměřte či klepněte pro detail.",
    "This measures initial data collection, not model trustworthiness. Continue validating forecasts and heating suggestions before enabling live control. Learning continues after initial data collection.": "Počáteční sběr není spolehlivost. Ověřte návrhy před řízením; učení pokračuje.",
    "History collection and learning paused because outdoor temperature is unavailable. Existing model parameters are retained.": "Historie a učení pozastaveny bez venkovní teploty. Model zůstává.",
    "No weather forecast: current outdoor temperature is held constant.": "Bez předpovědi počasí; venkovní teplota stálá.",
    "Live control awaits confirmation. Enable simulation, save, then disable it and confirm to activate thermostat control.": "Řízení čeká na potvrzení. Simulaci zapnout, uložit, pak vypnout a potvrdit.",
    "Waiting for enough heating and idle observations to estimate the remaining time.": "Čeká na více pozorování topení a klidu pro odhad.",
    "A door/window contact sensor can monitor the fireplace damper position. Select the sensor state that means the fireplace is in use. For a damper contact sensor, Open normally means active and Closed means inactive. Door/window labels are converted to Home Assistant’s underlying on/off values. Other sensors show their declared options, current valid state and any saved value. A contact state indicates the damper position; it does not prove that a fire is burning.": "Dveřní/okenní kontakt na klapce: Otevřeno obvykle aktivní, Zavřeno neaktivní. Uloženo on/off. Jiné senzory zobrazí možnosti. Poloha nedokazuje oheň.",
